**Proposed on:** 2 November 2026. **Replaces on acceptance:** [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/).
Desk acceptance has not been recorded. The accepted historical decision is preserved unchanged.

## Context

The [incident review](/kb/incidents/4471-review/) shows that one merged ticket contains separate parser and form-hint problems.
The existing triage prose uses normalized subjects, while its executable examples use tenant configuration and channel.
This can hide different bugs under one title and split the same bug across different titles.

## Proposed decision

Merge reports only when the available evidence establishes the same cause. Resolve tenant configuration and channel first;
for this product, use the locale order and form version in the supplied cause model. Read bodies for evidence that falls outside that model.
An unknown tenant or unexplained symptom stays separate for investigation. Deduplicate export rows by report ID before counting.

## Consequences

- The parser and booking-v3 hint receive separate engineering tickets and separate report counts.
- Subjects and browser tags help find reports but do not decide cause.
- Investigation takes more work at intake and prevents a second cause disappearing into a known ticket.
- Every page distinguishes reported symptoms, model-based classification, verified fixes, and remaining uncertainty.
- Computable counts stay in components; prose is reviewed against the rendered page and dated.

